cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the KINETIC custom kernel or any of the ideas presented here, please cite them as follows."
type: software
title: "KINETIC: KV-Informed Neural Inference and Token-Skipping Execution Core"
abstract: >
  KINETIC is a project with the aim of producing substantial wall-clock speedups on existing diffusion large-language models like Fast-dLLM v2 (NVIDIA).
  The framework integrates ideas of KV-caches, token-skipping policies, block-eviction policies, and custom Python kernels written in Triton to produce 
  substantial wall-clock speedups against Fast-dLLM v2 when run exclusively on a set of 10 NVIDIA RTX Pro 6000 GPUs (only one was used at a time).
